#!/bin/sh /etc/rc.common
#
# Copyright (C) 2026 Nexwall
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
#
# Superseded: both checks this script used to perform are now stale.
#
# 1. The [socket]/listen_path check protected ns-dpi-bridge, which read
#    netifyd's raw JSON socket output. ns-dpi-bridge is now retired (see
#    packages/ns-dpi/files/dpi-bridge.init) - none of the real plugins
#    (nx-proc-flows, nx-sink-http, nx-proc-aggregator, nx-proc-flow-actions)
#    use the [socket] mechanism at all.
# 2. The "autoconfig=0 with no internal_if/external_if" check treated that
#    combination as always broken and force-enabled autoconfig. It is now
#    the CORRECT, intentional state: the real design captures via NFQUEUE
#    (generic firewall chain hooks, see ns-netifyd-configure), not via
#    -I/-E interface flags at all - re-enabling autoconfig would incorrectly
#    "fix" a valid configuration, activating the vendor's own -I/-E
#    autodetect logic (which guesses a UCI network section named "wan" -
#    see msp/DPI_PLAN.md in the internal repo for why that guess is
#    frequently wrong here) alongside NFQUEUE, redundantly.
#
# Disabled, not removed: kept for reference/rollback.

START=49

start() {
	return 0
}
